<title>GERMANY: Henkel sees higher 1997 profit.</title>
<headline>Henkel sees higher 1997 profit.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemical concern Henkel KGaA said on Monday it expected its current year profit to be above that in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We are planning for a higher net profit in 1997 compared to 1996,&quot; Henkel chief Hans-Dietrich Winkhaus said at a news briefing. Last year, group net profit stood at 515 million marks ($303.7 million).</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.695 German Marks)</p>
